{%- comment -%}
JUMP NAV — a row of anchor links to sections further down the same page.
Add a list called `jump_nav` to a page's front matter:
  jump_nav:
    - label: "Vision & Mission"
      url: "#vision-mission"
    - label: "Meet the Team"
      url: "#meet-the-team"
Each url should be a #anchor matching an `id` you set on a section further
down (e.g. the `id` parameter on an info-blocks include).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if page.jump_nav -%}
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="On this page">
  <div class="container jump-nav-row">
    {% for item in page.jump_nav %}
      <a class="jump-nav-link" href="{% assign first_char = item.url | slice: 0 %}{% if item.url contains 'http' or first_char == '#' %}{{ item.url }}{% else %}{{ item.url | relative_url }}{% endif %}">{{ item.label }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</nav>
{%- endif -%}